2. What this repository does NOT contain
----------------------------------------

    The Pikmin 2 decompilation.  Not included, in whole or in fragments.
    setup.sh fetches it at build time; tools/prepare_source.py then copies
    the pinned revision into an ignored build directory and applies this
    port's changes there. The reference checkout is never modified.

    Note what follows from that: this port's changes to the game sources are
    expressed as Python transformations, not as diffs. Unlike a patch file,
    they carry no context lines, and so no excerpts of the decompiled
    sources appear in this repository at all.

    Aurora.  Fetched, not vendored. See section 3.

    Any game asset or data.  No textures, models, audio, video, text, level
    data, or executable code from the retail game is present in this
    repository in any form, compressed, encoded, or otherwise. A build is
    inert without a copy you supply yourself from your own disc.

    Not even a screenshot. Any image in the README shows this port rendering
    Nintendo's artwork, so it is hosted outside this repository and embedded
    by URL. Cloning this repository copies no image of the game to your disk.

    Any tool for obtaining game data.  No ripper, no downloader, no
    circumvention code, and no pointer to any.


